{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy fails: app paths not persisted to workspace",
    "Explanation": [
      "The three build jobs each generate an app file under app/\u003cplatform\u003e/, but their persist_to_workspace steps only persist the meta/\u003cplatform\u003e directories, not the app directories. The deploy job attaches the workspace and the job_6.log shows only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt, and ./meta/windows/build.txt present — no app files — so the `test -f app/...` checks fail with exit code 1. workflow_3.txt confirms all three build jobs succeeded (green) while deploy failed. The workspace did contain the meta files but not the apps, so it did not have the apps. Removing the verify step or changing attach_workspace would not make the apps appear, fixing one platform would still fail the other two tests, and store_artifacts must run in deploy per the requirement. The correct fix is to add the app/\u003cplatform\u003e paths to each build job's persist_to_workspace so the app files reach the deploy job."
