{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Add PostgreSQL to the CircleCI Job",
    "Explanation": [
      "The job starts only the circleci/node container; it never starts a PostgreSQL server [cite: 1]. The log confirms dockerize is installed and running, but nothing accepts connections at localhost:5432 [cite: 2]. Increasing the timeout or installing only a PostgreSQL client would not supply the missing server.",
      "",
      "Add a PostgreSQL service image alongside the Node image:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "docker:",
      "  - image: circleci/node",
      "  - image: postgres:16",
      "    environment:",
      "      POSTGRES_USER: app",
      "      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ci_test_password",
      "      POSTGRES_DB: app_test",
      "```",
      "",
      "CircleCI makes secondary service containers accessible through localhost. Keep the existing `dockerize -wait tcp://localhost:5432 -timeout 1m` step. Configure the Node application to connect to localhost on port 5432 using database app_test and the matching credentials above. These credentials are for the disposable CI database, not production. Starting the database service addresses the shown readiness failure."
